      <h1>China Battery Market: The 80% Manufacturing Concentration</h1>
      <p class="muted">Battery Market Intelligence · Data period 2024–2025 (varies by source) · Last reviewed 2026-09-15</p>

      <div class="box">
        <strong>Direct answer:</strong> The defining fact about China's battery market is not its dollar size — it is
        that China controls roughly <strong>80% of global lithium-ion manufacturing capacity</strong>. Demand is driven by
        electric vehicles and energy storage, and the same two leaders (<a href="https://manufacturer.worldbatteryhub.com/lithium-ev-manufacturers/">CATL and BYD</a>)
        sit at the centre of both production and innovation.
      </div>
      <h2>What is the battery technology mix?</h2>
      <p>Both chemistries at world scale — the largest lead-acid industry and the largest lithium industry, export-oriented.</p>

      <h2>Which manufacturers matter here?</h2>
      <p>CATL, BYD, EVE Energy, CALB, Camel, Tianneng and more — see the <a href="https://manufacturer.worldbatteryhub.com">manufacturer directory</a>.</p>

      <h2>Which regulations apply?</h2>
      <p>MIIT industrial policy, GB standards, and export/trade measures (see <a href="/battery-trade-hs-codes/">HS codes</a>).</p>

